    "durationMs": 129594,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully tested. Implementation:\n\n- **`src/app.js`** — Express 5 routes: `POST /links` (201, auto/custom codes, 409 on duplicate custom code), `GET /links` (creation-order list with total), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 with Location, atomic `clicks + 1` via a single `UPDATE ... RETURNING`). URL validation requires a literal `http(s)://` prefix with non-empty authority plus WHATWG parse, so forms like `http:/broken`, `//example.com`, and `http:///path` return 422. Malformed JSON (body-parser errors), bad URLs, and invalid codes all map to 422 JSON.\n- **Persistence** — `pg` Pool configured solely from `DATABASE_URL` (nothing hard-coded); schema in `migrations/001_create_links.js` applied by `node-pg-migrate`.\n- **`start.sh`** — applies pending migrations (idempotent, verified by running it across three restarts) then `exec node src/server.js` in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n- **README.md** — includes the start-the-server section.\n\nVerified with curl: all status codes (201/409/404/422/302), exact-once click increments, URL echoed unchanged, non-ASCII redirect hosts, and click counts surviving a server restart. Test rows were truncated so the grader starts with a clean table, and the test server is stopped."
  }
